  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "When a square of side length 2 units has its side length increased by $x$ units, the area increases by 12 square units. Find $x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=2$ units.",
      "worked": "The original area is $2^2=4$ square units and the new side length is $2+x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2+x)^2-4&=12\\\\x^2+4x+4-4&=12\\\\x^2+4x-12&=0\\\\(x+6)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=-6\\text{ or }2\\end{align*}$$\nReject $x=-6$ because the side length is increased. Hence $x=2$ units.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
